  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "If there is already some type of Antivirus or verified then you can disregard everything I say, today the thing that checks the avatar before sending is the vrchat SDK, but what no one wants to talk about is that this has been Bypass for a long time allowing you to upload any avatar or anything, it is possible to trick even the Oculos Quest 2 into running avatars that are extremely heavy and that would only work on the PC, but the real problem is not the people who do this but who use this loophole to upload avatars that are clearly malicious and if you are lucky you can find crackers, there should be something that scans the avatars that were uploaded and from worlds on the server and not leave it to an SDK that can be easily circumvented, It should There is a time when the avatar/world should be off before being available and in the meantime the avatar or world should be checked to see if it finds anything strange or malicious and then released and made available",
